  "description": "Manufacturer may substitute components with components of equal or greater performance level\n\nWhen it comes to trail riding, you can never go wrong with a hardtail. Hardtails are highly capable and versatile, so you can easily conquer the trails. Hardtails are even better when combined with ground eating 29 in. wheels and 2.4 in. gnarly MTB tires. The Colorado Comp has a lightweight and agile aluminum frame that uses 120mm of travel on the front suspension fork. It features a pro-grade Microshift 1 x 11 speed drive train with a 11-46T gear range that makes pedaling through technical terrain much easier.\n\nFeatures:\n\nAdult performance mountain bike\n\nLightweight 6061 aluminum frame with tapered head tube, internal cables, dropper post ready, replaceable derailleur hanger\n\nSturdy aluminum construction offers long-term durability\n\nTektro Hydraulic disc brakes offer reliable stopping power\n\nLightweight tubeless ready aluminum wheels with 27.5/29” x2.4” MTB cross-country tires offer reliable stopping power\n\nComfortable SR/Suntour XCM32 suspension fork with 120mm travel\n\nMicroShift XLE 11-46T wide range 1 x11 speed drivetrain helps provide smooth and efficient gear changes with a ratchet and pawl clutch\n\nBike weighs approximately 36 lbs.",
